:"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-29","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-09","committee":"Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-16","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-07","committee":"Joint Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-13","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":true,"url":"https://democratic.southoxon.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Disabled facilities grant underspend of \u00a31.1m being reviewed by Department of Health and Social Care","lead":"Central government scrutiny of DFG underspends signals potential policy risk; material capital budget underspend could indicate procurement capacity constraints or demand assumptions that do not hold","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Planning service lacks in-house capability, paying external consultants for planning appeals","lead":"Inability to resource core functions internally and reliance on expensive external consultants signals capability gaps and structural cost pressures","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Investment income outperformance of \u00a3899k entirely masks \u00a3714k service-level overspend, creating dependency on high interest rates","lead":"The council's positive reported position relies almost entirely on exceptional investment returns from a temporarily high interest rate environment. If and when rates fall, the underlying operational overspend becomes the actual problem","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","headline":"Disabled facilities grant underspend of \u00a31.1m being reviewed by Department of Health and Social Care","detail":"Council forecasts \u00a31.1m underspend on disabled facilities grant for the year based on Q1 run rate. The Department for Health and Social Care is currently reviewing DFG underspends nationally. Underspend will be profiled into future years.","category":"capital","matters":"Central government scrutiny of DFG underspends signals potential policy risk; material capital budget underspend could indicate procurement capacity constraints or demand assumptions that do not hold","figures":"\u00a31.1m underspend predicted on disabled facilities grant; approved capital programme \u00a343.632m with \u00a33.638m spent (8%) by end June","quote":"Disabled facilities grant is underspent and whilst spend will continue through the year, a \u00a31.1 million underspend against budget is predicted for this year based on the first quarter spend.  This underspend will be profiled into future years.  The Department for Health and Social Care are currently reviewing DFG underspends.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","headline":"Planning service lacks in-house capability, paying external consultants for planning appeals","detail":"Planning department is forecasting an overspend because it does not have the expertise to conduct planning appeals work in house and must engage external consultants instead.","category":"overspend","matters":"Inability to resource core functions internally and reliance on expensive external consultants signals capability gaps and structural cost pressures","figures":"Planning overspend as part of \u00a3714k total service-level overspend","quote":"Planning is forecasting an overspend as a result of using consultants for planning appeals.  The council does not have the expertise to do this work in house.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","headline":"Investment income outperformance of \u00a3899k entirely masks \u00a3714k service-level overspend, creating dependency on high interest rates","detail":"The council is forecasting \u00a37.2m investment income against budget of \u00a36.2m. Treasury deposits returned 4.56% versus SONIA benchmark of 3.74%. Without this \u00a3899k outperformance, the financial position would show a \u00a3715k overspend rather than a \u00a3184k underspend. The council holds \u00a355m of investments but achieved interest only from a high-rate environment.","category":"income","matters":"The council's positive reported position relies almost entirely on exceptional investment returns from a temporarily high interest rate environment. If and when rates fall, the underlying operational overspend becomes the actual problem","figures":"\u00a3899,000 additional investment income forecast; treasury deposit returns 4.56% versus 3.74% SONIA benchmark","quote":"The projected full year overspend at service level is forecast to be \u00a3714,000, and treasury income to be achieved in year is anticipated to be above budget by \u00a3899,000 leading to an overall net underspend of \u00a3184,000 at year end.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-07","committee":"Joint Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Internal audit annual report 2526","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s39657/39657.pdf","headline":"External quality assessment of internal audit function has not been completed, creating a regulatory compliance gap","detail":"The Global Internal Audit Standards (GIAS) require an external assessment of internal audit at least every five years. This requirement has not been met and was only added to the Quality Assurance and Improvement Programme (QAIP) during 2025/26. This means the audit function itself has not been independently verified for compliance or effectiveness.","category":"governance","matters":"Without independent external verification, there is reduced assurance that the internal audit function is itself operating effectively and providing reliable oversight of controls.","figures":"External assessment requirement: every 5 years; no assessment completed in last 5+ years","quote":"It is a requirement of the standards for an external assessment of internal audit to be completed at least every five years. An external assessment has not been undertaken within the last five years and has been added to the QAIP, which is regularly presented to JAGC for review.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-07","committee":"Joint Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Internal audit annual report 2526","paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s39657/39657.pdf","headline":"Resource constraints within the internal audit team caused the council to miss one of three performance targets and left five audits incomplete as of end of June","detail":"The council achieved only 2 of 3 performance targets in 2025/26. Performance Target 3 (completing fieldwork on 80% of operational audits) was achieved at only 74%, with five operational audits still in progress on 26 June. The report attributes delays to 'audits taking longer than budgeted, the need to await the completion of an internal investigation before finalising one audit and resource constraints within the team'.","category":"governance","matters":"Under-resourced audit function means the council may not be identifying all control weaknesses or risk areas, reducing the comprehensiveness of the control environment assessment.","figures":"2 of 3 performance targets met; 5 operational audits in progress; PT3 achieved at 74% vs 80% target","quote":"The reasons for the delay in completing these audits include audits taking longer than budgeted, the need to await the completion of an internal investigation before finalising one audit and resource constraints within the team.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"South Oxfordshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Disabled facilities grant underspend of \u00a31.1m being reviewed by Department of Health and Social Care","lead":"Central government scrutiny of DFG underspends signals potential policy risk; material capital budget underspend could indicate procurement capacity constraints or demand assumptions that do not hold","also":["2 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-21","n_findings":3,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"3. SOUTH budget monitoring report June 2026","top_paper_url":"https://southoxon.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s40392/40392.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":44,"news_drafts_total":3}}